            <ArticleTitle>Rhabdomyolysis following status asthmaticus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>409-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 15-year-old Chinese boy developed rhabdomyolysis with myoglobinuria and marked elevation of serum creatine phosphokinase following a prolonged and severe attack of asthma. He recovered after vigorous hydration and supportive treatment. Clinicians should be aware of this potentially fatal, albeit rare, complication of status asthmaticus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
